<title>GERMANY: Bayer 9-mo group pre-tax profit 3.7 bln dmk.</title>
<headline>Bayer 9-mo group pre-tax profit 3.7 bln dmk.</headline>
<dateline>LEVERKUSEN, Germany 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     3,701   vs 3,304</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   2,300   up 18 pct</p>
<p>    Group sales				  36,544  vs 34,027</p>
<p>    Parent pre-tax profit		    1,850   vs 1,640</p>
<p>    Parent sales				 14,064  vs 14,060</p>
<p>    Group foreign sales			23,674  vs 21,495</p>
<p>    Group domestic sales		     12,870  vs 12,532</p>
<p>    Group personnel costs		    11,213  vs 10,889</p>
<p>    Group workforce (Sept 30)		142,100 vs 142,900</p>
<p>    Parent personnel costs		   4,587   vs 4,599</p>
<p>    Parent workforce (Sept 30)	     48,076  vs 49,985</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts forecast Bayer's nine-month pre-tax profit would range between 3.68 and 3.78 billion marks, showing an average 13 percent rise. Sales meanwhile were expected to show a rise of on average 7.3 percent, ranging between 36.24 and 36.75 billion marks.</p>
<p>Full name of German chemicals and drugs group is Bayer AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
